  <h2>Seoul's Outdoor Living Room</h2>
  <p>The Han River (한강) runs through the heart of Seoul for 41km. Its parks are where Seoulites escape the city — for picnics, cycling, sports, or simply watching the skyline at dusk. For visitors, the Han River offers a completely different side of Seoul: relaxed, scenic, and deeply local.</p>

  <h2>Han River Cruise</h2>
  <p>A night cruise on the Han River is one of Seoul's most memorable experiences. Boats depart from Yeouido Ferry Terminal with spectacular views of Seoul's skyline, especially after dark when the city lights up. The Banpo Bridge Rainbow Fountain — the world's longest bridge fountain — is the highlight.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Duration: 60–90 minutes</li>
    <li>Options: Daytime sightseeing, sunset dinner cruise, night party cruise</li>
    <li>Departure: Yeouido, Ttukseom, or Jamsil Ferry Terminals</li>
  </ul>

